WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.890
Look at the far right of the periodic
table: group 18, the noble gases.

2
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.470
Neon, argon, krypton.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.390
Each has eight electrons
in its outer level.

4
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:16.930
And then, at the very top, sits helium,
with just two electrons in total.

5
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:21.950
So why is helium in group 18 when
its atoms have only two electrons?

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.390
In this mission, you'll read
the periodic table's periods,

7
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:30.810
groups and blocks, and sort elements
into metals, metalloids and non-metals.

8
00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.610
You'll go from an element's position to
its electron configuration, and back again.

9
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:39.890
Your mission: explain why
helium belongs in group 18.
